/* 签文（分享句） */
body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-verse {
  margin: 30px 0 0;
  padding: 22px 18px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--ggw-line);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ggw-line);
  text-align: center;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-verse blockquote {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: clamp(18px, 5vw, 22px);
  letter-spacing: .18em;
  line-height: 1.9;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-energy {
  margin: 26px 2px 0;
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 2;
  letter-spacing: .03em;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-reading {
  margin: 14px 2px 0;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ggw-ink) 88%, var(--ggw-ink-soft));
  font-size: 14.5px;
  line-height: 2.1;
  text-align: justify;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-cols {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 22px 26px;
  margin: 30px 2px 0;
  padding-top: 24px;
  border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ggw-line) 70%, transparent);
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-col h3 {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  color: var(--ggw-dai);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: .4em;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-col p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ggw-ink-soft);
  font-size: 13.5px;
  line-height: 1.95;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-col ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  color: var(--ggw-ink-soft);
  font-size: 13.5px;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-col li {
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  padding-left: 14px;
  position: relative;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-col li::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: .62em;
  width: 5px;
  height: 5px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ggw-dai) 55%, transparent);
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-actions {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 12px 26px;
  margin: 34px 2px 0;
}

body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-disclaimer {
  margin-top: 30px;
  padding-top: 16px;
  border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ggw-line) 60%, transparent);
  font-size: 11.5px;
  opacity: .8;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- 窄屏 ---- */
@media (max-width: 420px) {
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw { padding: 18px 16px 40px; }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-gate-form { flex-direction: column; }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-slip { padding: 15px 14px; }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-verdict { padding: 24px 18px 28px; }
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- 动效偏好 ---- */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-slip,
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-dot.now,
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-loading-ring,
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-slip.stamped .ggw-slip-seal {
    animation: none;
  }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-slip.stamped .ggw-slip-seal {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1);
  }
  body[data-skin="grand-view-garden"] .ggw-slip { transition: none; }
}

part.text:
Now write a garden skin test: tools/test-garden-skin.mjs. It should:
1. Import the real skin module: `await import("../deploy-ready/themes/grand-view-garden/skin.js")`.
2. Check views exist for all 5 pages, id matches.
3. Render each view with contexts and assert HTML contains key markers (no default template classes like .topbar, uses .ggw classes).
4. Drive the real app.js end-to-end with __MYTHIC_SKINS__ preset (imported real module), a DOM stub — reuse smoke-h5's stub? That's a big file. Simpler: build a minimal but functional flow — actually I can reuse smoke-h5.mjs's stub by... it's not exported. Copying the whole DOM stub would be ~200 lines duplicated.

Alternative: make the garden e2e test import the stub from smoke-h5? smoke-h5.mjs runs tests on import (side effects). Not clean.

Option: write the garden test as a variant of smoke-h5 that sets DSH_SKIN env? Rather than duplicating, I could parametrize smoke-h5 with env vars: DSH_SMOKE_TEST_ID and DSH_SMOKE_THEME... That modifies smoke-h5 more invasively. Hmm.

Actually simpler approach for e2e garden flow: modify smoke-h5.mjs minimally to support a "skin test mode" via env: when DSH_SMOKE_SKIN=grand-view-garden, it:
- loads the real skin module and sets globalThis.__MYTHIC_SKINS__ before evaluating app.js
- stubs fetch with product_id "grand-view-garden", content for garden theme (productThemes("grand-view-garden")), 18 questions
- runs the same flow with different assertions? That doubles complexity of smoke-h5.

Better: write tools/test-garden-skin.mjs self-contained with its own compact DOM stub focused on the skin flow. The stub needs: document.querySelector/#app, body.setAttribute, innerHTML parse enough for querySelectorAll(".ggw-slip") etc, addEventListener, localStorage, fetch stub, matchMedia absent, window.setTimeout, import works via preset __MYTHIC_SKINS__ (no dynamic import needed).

The parse requirement: app.js trySkinView does `app.innerHTML = html` — my stub needs the app element's innerHTML setter, and bind uses root.querySelector("#ggw-gate-code") etc. But wait — bind receives `app` — the SAME app element whose innerHTML was set. So querySelector must parse the innerHTML. smoke-h5 has a parser (~130 lines). For garden test I need querySelector with id/class selectors and querySelectorAll for .ggw-slip, .ggw-dot, buttons.

Rather than duplicating 200 lines, extract? Modifying smoke-h5 to export its stub utilities — smoke-h5 currently executes tests at top level on import; I'd need to guard with import.meta.url check... that changes the file structure.

Cleanest: write a standalone test with a compact custom stub (~100 lines) — parser subset: build tree from HTML with a regex-based tokenizer; support class/id selectors, tag selectors, [disabled] attr maybe. The skin HTML is simpler than greek's. Elements needed:
- #ggw-gate-code input, #ggw-gate-submit button (gate)
- #ggw-enter (cover)
- .ggw-slip buttons with dataset.i (question), #ggw-prev, #ggw-exit
- result: #ggw-copy, #ggw-share, #ggw-again, #ggw-home; .ggw-verdict-name text
- .ggw-dot count = 18
- brandBar text check

click() → dispatch listeners. app.js view binding uses addEventListener — my stub supports it.

Flow assertions:
1. gate view renders skin (has .ggw-gate-title 入园, no .gate-hero default).
2. submit code → cover skin (大观园回声 + #ggw-enter).
3. click enter → Q1 with 第一试... "第一景", 18 dots, 3 slips.
4. click slip 0 → after 320ms advances to Q2 (第二景).
5. prev works: click 回看上一景 → back to Q1 with slip stamped.
6. Run all 18 → resultLoading then result: verdict name present, seal, verse share_line, 4 action links.
7. share button calls drawShareImage — needs canvas stub with getContext returning object with methods... drawShareImage uses canvas.getContext("2d"), fillText etc, canvas.toBlob. Stub: getContext returns a Proxy that no-ops all methods; toBlob(cb) → cb(null) fine (returns early). document.createElement("canvas") must return that. Manageable.
8. copy uses navigator.clipboard — ctx.actions.copy → copyResult → navigator.clipboard.writeText. Stub navigator.clipboard. And button text changes.
9. CSS scoping check: every selector in skin.css starts with body[data-skin= or is @keyframes/@media — regex check. And every class used in skin.js templates (ggw-*) exists in skin.css? Reverse: every ggw-* class referenced in CSS exists in JS or vice versa — loose check: classes in JS ⊆ classes in CSS ∪ {ra, ra-fill} (SVG classes). Good check.
10. Greek isolation: ensure default app still renders greek gate when no skin (already covered by smoke-h5) — skip.
11. Check app.js untouched default templates: assert skin CSS classes never referenced in default app.js templates (no "ggw-" in default views) — trivially true.
12. Assert __MYTHIC_SKINS__ cleanup after test (globalThis delete) to not affect anything else. Same process only.

Also assert: skin.js has no fetch/import of server content, no "scores" string (no scoring logic), does not reference quiz_content_upgrade.json.

Also the escapeHtml check: esc() applied — verify question text with special chars escaped? Data has no HTML chars; check esc function exists by unit-calling? esc not exported. Skip.

DOM stub design (compact):

```js
function parseHtml(html) { // returns array of nodes
  // tokenizer: tags and text
}
```

I'll write a small recursive parser: match /<\/?([a-zA-Z][^\s>]*)((?:\s+[\w-]+(?:="[^"]*")?)*)\s*\/?>/ and text nodes. Track void elements (br, img, input, i? no i has content... void: input, br, img, hr, meta, link). Build El objects: tagName, id, className set, children, dataset, listeners, attributes.

El.querySelector(selector): support comma? Not needed. Support "#id", ".class", "tag", ".class#id"? Keep: split selector into tokens: tag + (#id)? + (.classes)*. Depth-first search.

innerHTML setter on app: parse html into children.

document = { querySelector: (sel) => sel === "#app" ? appEl : search document tree? app.js only uses document.querySelector("#app") at module init, then document.querySelectorAll("[data-art]")... only in default greek flow. document.createElement, document.body (El), document.title. window = { setTimeout, matchMedia absent, __cardMotionTimers }. localStorage stub. navigator = { clipboard: { writeText: async () => {} }, userAgent... } — deviceFingerprint uses navigator/screen/Intl — navigator.userAgent etc must exist: provide minimal. screen {width,height,colorDepth}. location: { pathname: "/t/grand-view-garden", search: "" }.

fetch stub: /api/redeem, /api/verify-license, /api/content (garden sanitized), /api/score (real selectWinner on garden theme).

Garden content: productThemes("grand-view-garden") + sanitizeTheme → { product: {...}, themes: [...] }.

Answers: 18 zeros → selectWinner real scoring.mjs.

The preset: globalThis.__MYTHIC_SKINS__ = { "grand-view-garden": (await import skin module).default } — test file is ESM (.mjs), can top-level await import. app.js run via new Function — dynamic import not triggered since preset found. loadSkin: presetSkins returns preset → adoptSkin(skin) — adoptSkin touches document.title — my stub document needs title setter (plain property fine).

initApp: state.testId = currentTestId() → location.pathname /t/grand-view-garden → match. loadSkin → skin set. stored license null → renderGate → trySkinView gate.

Timing: app.js at end calls initApp() — async. Then await sleep(50). Then flow.

After click slip: window.setTimeout(320) — my stub window.setTimeout = real setTimeout. await sleep(400).

click enter → start → renderQuestion → sleep.

Note: app.js's `document.body.removeAttribute("data-skin")` in shell — default flow only. trySkinView sets body.setAttribute("data-skin", ...) — assert body attributes.

Also result flow: renderResult → trySkinView("resultLoading") — needs `app` innerHTML — fine; then fetch /api/score → then trySkinView("result"). The payload includes full result record (with reading etc.) from my stub: theme.results.find(winner). Good.

Buttons: El.click() → run listeners stored via addEventListener("click", fn) — my bind uses addEventListener exclusively in skin; app.js view code uses addEventListener for slips too. dispatch: fn({}) — handlers don't use event object much (slip handler no event use; gate input keydown uses event.key — skip).

canvas: document.createElement("canvas") → El with getContext(){ return proxy } — share test: click #ggw-share → ctx.actions.share() → skin.share({result,...}) → drawShareImage → canvas.getContext("2d") → proxy; ctx2d.font setters fine on proxy (set ok); measureText not used in skin's drawShareImage (no wrapText). textAlign set fine. canvas.toBlob → cb(null) → if (!blob) return. Good. Proxy needs get → function returning undefined; but properties like globalAlpha assigned — proxy set trap default ok. Use new Proxy({}, { get: () => () => {} }) — but `ctx2d.fillStyle = INK` set on target fine.

toBlob on El canvas: define method on created canvas element.

Let me also double-check skin gate submit flow: ctx.submit → getLicense() → localStorage.getItem — my localStorage stub returns null. api("/api/redeem", ...) → global fetch stub → returns { ok: true, secret: "...", firstUse: true, product_id: "grand-view-garden", product_name: "大观园回声测试" } → saveLicense → product match → loadContent() (async, not awaited — fire and forget) → returns {type:"unlocked"}. loadContent fetches /api/content → sets quizData → home() → themes.length === 1 → cover() → trySkinView cover. await sleep after submit click → cover rendered. Good.

Score answers: all zeros — selectWinner handles.

One more check in app.js result context: copyText — state.skin.copyText exists. copyResult(result, override) — navigator.clipboard.writeText then button.textContent = "已复制" — wait, that sets textContent on #copy button — but that's the DEFAULT view's button id! In skin flow, ctx.actions.copy → copyResult → `document.querySelector("#copy")` → null → error caught in try? `button.textContent = ...` — button is null → TypeError → caught by try/catch in copyResult? Let me re-read copyResult:

```js
async function copyResult(result, textOverride) {
  const text = textOverride || `...`;
  const button = document.querySelector("#copy");
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
    button.textContent = "已复制";
  } catch (error) { ... }
  window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = "复制结果文案"; }, 1800);
}
```

The setTimeout callback references button.textContent — if button null → throws inside setTimeout → unhandled error. In skin flow #copy doesn't exist (skin uses #ggw-copy). The writeText succeeds, then `button.textContent = "已复制"` throws INSIDE try → caught → button.textContent again throws inside catch?? No — catch block does console.error and button.textContent = "请手动复制" → throws again → uncaught. This is a real bug for skin flow. Fix copyResult: guard button null:

```js
async function copyResult(result, textOverride) {
  const text = textOverride || ...;
  const button = document.querySelector("#copy");
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
    if (button) button.textContent = "已复制";
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to copy result:", error);
    if (button) button.textContent = "请手动复制";
  }
  if (button) window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = "复制结果文案"; }, 1800);
}
```

Wait but in test my document.querySelector searches document tree — #copy doesn't exist → null → guard needed. Fix in app.js.

Also shareResult default: skin share overrides — fine.

Now write the test file. Also fix copyResult guard first.

Parser: I need classList? bind code uses classList.add/remove on slip. My El needs classList add/remove/contains. Slip has class "ggw-slip stamped" — parse class attr into set.

dataset.i from data-i attr — parse data-* into dataset.

Also pathDots uses <i> elements with class ggw-dot.

Disabled attr on prev button — attribute presence; test asserts prev.disabled? I'll check attribute disabled present when index 0. My El: disabled property? bind doesn't set disabled; render template includes `disabled` attr for index 0. For the test assert attributes.disabled.

Note in question bind: prev listener attached always (even disabled attr) — clicking disabled in real browser no event; in test I just won't click when disabled.

